  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Laos National Chamber of Commerce and Industry (LNCCI) adopted a new 6-pillar Strategic Plan 2021-25 in December 2020. The LNCCI Strategic Plan aims to widen representation, especially among SMEs, and enhance their service provision. The implementation of the strategy was launched through various new services such as SME clinic, OSH trainings, industry-academy cooperative training helpdesks, job fairs and by offering an MBA course together with universities to meet the changing needs of members and potential members. In addition, LNCCI developed key performance indicators for the new strategy to expand membership and adapted its organizational structure of Bureau for Employer&apos;s Activities (BEA) in response to changes in organizational needs. The organization has been restructured to recognize the BEA as an important part of the LNCCI&apos;s mandate as a result of the strategic plan, placing Lao Business Forum, the biggest annual economic policy dialogue with Prime Minister and Ministers, under the BEA. In line with the Prime Minister&apos;s new Decree 237 of 18 May 2020, LNCCI revised its operating principles, functions and mandate to strengthen its role as the representative employer&apos;s organization on labour and social policy. 
In order to enhance its capacity to manage its organization and support its members, LNCCI strengthened the capacity of board/staff members of LNCCI, provincial chapters and business associations to perform more effectively through skills development of key personnel and provide services for member companies. 
LNCCI further implemented its new strategic plan by launching the MSME COVID-19 Online Talks in July 2021 and MSME COVID-19 Help Desk in August 2021 to support MSMEs that are searching for information about available COVID-19 support and that would like assistance in applying for finance. 18 episodes were broadcasted through Online Talks in 2021. To support the implementation of LNCCI&apos;s strategic plan on enhancing its services, the ILO translated ITCILO guidebooks on the Effective Employers&apos; Organization, a series of &quot;hands-on&quot; guides to building and managing effective employers&apos; organizations, in the Lao language. 

The ILO further organized a workshop to examine, benchmark and evaluate new services for LNCCI. Additionally, the ILO offered a training workshop for LNCCI board/staff members, 17 provincial chapters and 27 sectoral business associations to strengthen their capacity to provide direct services to their member companies in December 2020. After the workshop, LNCCI formed peer support group and structure of support.

With the support of Japan Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare, the ILO also held a capacity building training of advisory services on labour law, international labour standards and social dialogue in May 2021 for LNCCI and provincial chapter board/staff members with a view to strengthening their abilities as employer&apos;s organizations. 

With the support of the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation, the ILO supported the development of the MSME COVID-19 Online Talks and MSME COVID-19 Help Desk.</narrative>
   </description>
